# SRG-APP-000123-AU-000150  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must protect audit tools from unauthorized
# deletion.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000123-AU-000150
group:           V-221919
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-001495
control_rev5:    AU-9

contribution:    Deleting a saved search, report or configuration object that serves as an
                 audit tool requires write access to it or the capability that bypasses
                 access control lists, so the application's share is that this capability
                 stays off the general-purpose roles.

governs:         authorize.conf - Used to create roles.

check:           authorize.conf [role_user] admin_all_objects absent
check:           authorize.conf [role_power] admin_all_objects absent

external:        Delete permissions on the Splunk binaries and installation directories -
                 SPLK-CL-000190 implements this at the operating system layer
external:        Object-level write access recorded in default.meta, which the btool-based
                 collector does not read

citation:        restmap.conf capability.delete present is removed for the reason given on
                 SRG-APP-000121-AU-000130 - the stanza exists only where an app declares
                 its own REST endpoint, so the condition fails a conformant deployment that
                 declares none. admin_all_objects absent over [role_<roleName>] fails every
                 install because the shipped role_admin holds it (authorize.conf:290);
                 pinned to the two shipped general-purpose roles it passes stock and fails
                 a real grant.
finding:         A general-purpose role holds admin_all_objects, so the objects that serve
                 as audit tools can be deleted by an account that is not privileged.
